  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "eIn Fedora 5.1.0 we had the repository.json (a modeshape-ism) which provided a single location for configuring Fedora.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In Fedora 6.0.0 we are using system properties for configuration passed via the command line.  It would be nice to have a single location for all config rather than a peppering of system properties.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "What does the configuration need to contain? Here's a starting list",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "jdbc config for indices",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "storage location (mount point, cloud storage configuration)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "other settings (such as auto versioning)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "orderedList"
    }
   ],
