  "description": "<p>eIn Fedora 5.1.0 we had the repository.json (a modeshape-ism) which provided a single location for configuring Fedora.</p>\n\n<p>In Fedora 6.0.0 we are using system properties for configuration passed via the command line.  It would be nice to have a single location for all config rather than a peppering of system properties.</p>\n\n<p>What does the configuration need to contain? Here's a starting list</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>jdbc config for indices</li>\n\t<li>storage location (mount point, cloud storage configuration)</li>\n\t<li>other settings (such as auto versioning)</li>\n</ol>\n",
